-- title:
--   From smooth-point stalks to smooth-point packages (q=2)
-- statement:
--   **Setting.** Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $q=2$, $M'$ is a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and $\ell_g$ is a prime with $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g \mid M'$ (a rigidity guard on the level). Further, $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ satisfying `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$.
--
--   The finite set $W$ consists of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` over the residue field of $A$, and `hW` identifies $W$ with `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`: the places $w$ that are rational (the structure map from the base field to the residue field of $w$ is surjective), are affine geometric places, and whose value `w.evalAt (jGeomGen …)` lies in the supersingular $j$-set `ssJSet q`. An element $s \in W$ is fixed. The hypothesis `hle` records the inclusion `modularFunctionFieldBar M' ≤ fieldBar q M'` of the base change to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the full level-$M'$ modular function field into $\bar F :=$ `fieldBar q M'`, the base change to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the $X_H$-function field of level $q^2M'$ for $H =$ `levelH q M'`, both realised inside Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. The datum $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'`, that is: a valuation subring `R₀.integers` of the source, a surjective residue homomorphism onto the target whose kernel is the maximal ideal, compatibility with $A \to$ `ResidueField A` on constants, the scaling property that every nonzero element can be multiplied by a constant so as to have nonzero residue, and a degree-preserving map on places compatible with order functions on divisors. The hypothesis `hR₀` states that for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that image belongs to `R₀.integers` and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over `ResidueField A`, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   **Small-field data.** $k_0$ is an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0$ has image in $A$; the hypotheses `hdvr`, `hunif`, `hhens`, `hres` say that $A \cap k_0$ (the comap of $A$ along $k_0 \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$) is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, is henselian local, and has algebraically closed residue field; `hκ` says that every $a \in A$ differs from some element of $k_0 \cap A$ by an element of the maximal ideal of $A$.
--
--   **Auxiliary constants.** $\ell$ is a prime with $3 \le \ell$, $\ell \ne q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$; $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$; and $\varpi_t \in k_0$ has image in $A$ with $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$.
--
--   **Layers.** $\iota$ is a type indexing intermediate fields $K_n$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/k_0$, each finite-dimensional over $k_0$ (`hKfin`), together with valuation subrings $A_n$ of $K_n$ characterised by $x \in A_n \iff x \in A$ (`hAn`).
--
--   **Quantifiers of the conclusion.** The conclusion is stated with $\bar F$ regarded as a $k_0$-algebra through $k_0 \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}} \to \bar F$. It asserts, for every intermediate field $F_0$ of $\bar F/k_0$ with $k_0(\,\mathrm{im}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}} \to \bar F)\,) \sqcup F_0 = \bar F$, for every field $\mathrm{FSS}$ which is an algebra over `ResidueField A`, for every `RegularProlongation` $R$ of $A$ from $\bar F$ to $\mathrm{FSS}$ (a valuation subring `R.integers` of $\bar F$ with a surjective residue map onto $\mathrm{FSS}$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal, restricting to $A$ on constants and with the scaling property), and for every finite set $N$ of places of $\mathrm{FSS}$ over `ResidueField A` and every family of data
--   $$S_n(Q,\cdot),\qquad \varphi_n(Q,\cdot) : A_n[T] \to S_n(Q,n),\qquad \chi_n(Q,\cdot) : S_n(Q,n) \to \mathrm{ResidueField}\,A,\qquad D_n(Q,\cdot)$$
--   indexed by places $Q$ of $\mathrm{FSS}$ and by $n : \iota$ — with $S_n(Q,n)$ a subring of $\bar F$, $\varphi_n$ a ring homomorphism from the polynomial ring over $A_n$, $\chi_n$ a ring homomorphism to the residue field of $A$, and $D_n(Q,n)$ a set of places of $\bar F$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ — that the *stalk* conditions below imply the *package* conditions below.
--
--   **The stalk hypothesis.** It is the conjunction of: $\#N = q+1$; the layerwise clauses, holding for every place $Q \notin N$ and every $n : \iota$, namely (i) surjectivity of $A_n \to \mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$, $a \mapsto \mathrm{res}_A(a)$; (ii) the image of $A_n$ in $\bar F$ lies in $S_n(Q,n)$; (iii) $\varphi_n(Q,n)$ is formally smooth and formally unramified; (iv) $\varphi_n(Q,n)(C\,a)$ equals the image of $a$ in $\bar F$; (v) $\chi_n(Q,n)(\varphi_n(Q,n)(C\,a)) = \mathrm{res}_A(a)$; (vi) $\chi_n(Q,n)(\varphi_n(Q,n)(X)) = 0$; (vii) for every $c \in A_n$ with $\mathrm{res}_A(c) = 0$ there is a unique ring homomorphism $\chi : S_n(Q,n) \to A_n$ which is an $A_n$-section of $\varphi_n(Q,n) \circ C$, reduces to $\chi_n(Q,n)$, and sends $\varphi_n(Q,n)(X)$ to $c$; (viii) every $f \in S_n(Q,n)$ lies in `R.integers`, its $R$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $Q$, and the residue there of that $R$-residue is the image of $\chi_n(Q,n)(f)$ in the residue field of $Q$; (ix) $\varphi_n(Q,n)(X)$ lies in `R.integers` and its $R$-residue has order $1$ at $Q$; (x) $P \in D_n(Q,n)$ holds precisely when $P$ is rational, every $f \in S_n(Q,n)$ lies in the valuation subring of $P$ with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f) \in A$, and for every such $f$ one has $A$-valuation of $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)$ less than $1$ if and only if $\chi_n(Q,n)(f) = 0$; (xi) $\varphi_n(Q,n)(X) \ne \varphi_n(Q,n)(C\,c)$ for all $c \in A_n$; (xii) $S_n(Q,n)$ is local with maximal ideal the kernel of $\chi_n(Q,n)$, Noetherian, and a unique factorisation monoid; (xiii) $S_n(Q,n)$ is contained in $L_n := k_0(\mathrm{im}\,K_n) \sqcup F_0$; (xiv) every element of $L_n$ is a quotient $g/h$ with $g,h \in S_n(Q,n)$, $h \ne 0$; (xv) linear disjointness: for a finite family $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ linearly independent over $K_n$ and $a_i \in L_n$, the relation $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$ forces all $a_i = 0$; (xvi) for every $A_n$-section $\chi$ of $\varphi_n(Q,n) \circ C$ reducing to $\chi_n(Q,n)$, the kernel of $\chi$ is generated by $\varphi_n(Q,n)(X) - \varphi_n(Q,n)(C(\chi(\varphi_n(Q,n)(X))))$; (xvii) there is a generator $\varpi$ of the maximal ideal of $A_n$, nonzero, with $\varphi_n(Q,n)(C\,\varpi)$ prime in $S_n(Q,n)$, such that for $f \in L_n$ one has $f \in$ `R.integers` if and only if $f = g/h$ with $g,h \in S_n(Q,n)$ and $\varphi_n(Q,n)(C\,\varpi) \nmid h$, and such that for every prime $p$ of $S_n(Q,n)$ not associated to $\varphi_n(Q,n)(C\,\varpi)$ and every $x \in S_n(Q,n)$ there is a monic $r \in A_n[T]$ with $p$ dividing the value at $x$ of $r$ pushed forward along $\varphi_n(Q,n) \circ C$; (xviii) finite generation up to units: there is a finite subset $G$ of $S_n(Q,n)$ such that every $f \in S_n(Q,n)$ satisfies $fh = g$ with $g,h$ in the subring generated by $G$ together with the image of $A_n$, and $h$ the image of a unit of $S_n(Q,n)$. Further conjuncts of the hypothesis: the layer compatibilities, namely that $K_n \le K_{n'}$ implies $S_n(Q,n) \le S_n(Q,n')$, that then $S_n(Q,n')$ lies in the subring generated by $S_n(Q,n)$ together with the image of $A_{n'}$, that $\varphi_n(Q,n)(X)$ has one and the same image in $\bar F$ for all $n,n'$, and that $\chi_n(Q,n')$ restricts to $\chi_n(Q,n)$; disc disjointness: for $Q,Q' \notin N$, any $n$ and any place $P$ lying in both $D_n(Q,n)$ and $D_n(Q',n)$, one has $Q = Q'$; cusp avoidance: for $Q \notin N$, every $n$ and every $P \in D_n(Q,n)$, the order at $P$ of the image in $\bar F$ of the $q$-expansion `jq` of $j$ (transported along `hle`) is $\ge 0$; and level equivariance: for every $\tau$ in the subgroup of $\mathrm{Aut}(\bar F/\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ generated by the automorphisms `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` with $\zeta$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, and every proof $h_\tau$ that $\tau$ preserves `R.integers`, and every place $Q$ of $\mathrm{FSS}$: $(\mathrm{resAut}\,\tau) \cdot Q \in N$ if and only if $Q \in N$, and if $Q \notin N$ then for every $n$ the translated disc $\{P : \tau^{-1}\cdot P \in D_n(Q,n)\}$ equals $D_n((\mathrm{resAut}\,\tau)\cdot Q, n)$.
--
--   **The package conclusion.** Under these hypotheses the same data satisfy: $\#N = q+1$; and for every place $Q \notin N$, first, for every $n : \iota$, the clauses (i)–(x) above hold verbatim, and in addition
--
--   (a) for every ring homomorphism $\chi : S_n(Q,n) \to A_n$ which is an $A_n$-section of $\varphi_n(Q,n)\circ C$ and reduces to $\chi_n(Q,n)$, there is a unique place $P \in D_n(Q,n)$ with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f) = \chi(f)$ for all $f \in S_n(Q,n)$;
--
--   (b) for every $P \in D_n(Q,n)$ and every $f \in L_n = k_0(\mathrm{im}\,K_n) \sqcup F_0$: $f$ lies in the valuation subring of $P$ if and only if $f = g/h$ with $g,h \in S_n(Q,n)$ and $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(h) \ne 0$;
--
--   (c) unit principle: every nonzero $f \in L_n$ whose order vanishes at all $P \in D_n(Q,n)$ satisfies $c f = u$ in $\bar F$ for some nonzero $c \in K_n$ and some unit $u$ of $S_n(Q,n)$;
--
--   (d) locality: every $f \in L_n$ which lies in `R.integers` and in the valuation subring of every $P \in D_n(Q,n)$ lies in $S_n(Q,n)$;
--
--   (e) the finite generation up to units (xviii);
--
--   and second, the layer compatibilities (monotonicity $S_n(Q,n) \le S_n(Q,n')$ for $K_n \le K_{n'}$, generation of $S_n(Q,n')$ by $S_n(Q,n)$ and the image of $A_{n'}$, the common image of $\varphi_n(Q,n)(X)$, and compatibility of the $\chi_n$) exactly as in the hypothesis. Finally the conclusion repeats the disc disjointness, the cusp avoidance (nonnegativity of the order of $j$ on each disc) and the level equivariance conjuncts in the same form as in the hypothesis.
--
--   Thus the clauses (xi)–(xvii) of the stalk hypothesis — non-constancy of the coordinate, the local Noetherian factorial structure, containment in and generation of $L_n$, linear disjointness, the kernel description, and the uniformiser with the description of `R.integers` and the branch-finiteness — are consumed and replaced in the conclusion by the four statements (a)–(d) describing $D_n(Q,n)$ as the set of $A_n$-sections, the valuation subrings of its points in terms of $S_n(Q,n)$, the unit principle and the locality of sections.
--
--   This is the functorial upgrade step, in the case $q = 2$ at a rigid auxiliary level, from layerwise smooth-point stalk data on the supersingular part of the full-level modular curve over the valuation ring $A$ above $q$ to full smooth-point package data, in which residue discs are identified with the sets of $A_n$-valued sections of the stalks. It feeds the construction of the semistable model at level $q^2M'$, being cited by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.supersingularProlongation_ends_residueDiscs_cover_of_affineChart_poles_hasse_commonChart_nodes_of_eq_two_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.supersingularProlongation_ends_residueDiscs_cover_of_affineChart_poles_hasse_commonChart_nodes_of_eq_two_of_dvd), and rests on the general locality principle [`AlgebraicCurve.RegularProlongation.disc_sections_locality_of_smoothPoint`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.RegularProlongation.disc_sections_locality_of_smoothPoint) for regular prolongations of curves.
